no-ai-slop
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes rule definitions derived from no-ai-slop
(https://github.com/petergyang/no-ai-slop), Copyright (c) 2026 Peter Yang,
licensed under the MIT License.

The word list split across Voices/Banned.yml and Voices/InflatedWords.yml, and
the patterns in Voices/BinaryContrast.yml, Voices/ThroatClearing.yml,
Voices/Puffery.yml, Voices/Weasel.yml, Voices/Recap.yml,
Voices/SuperficialAnalysis.yml, Voices/ColonReveal.yml and
Voices/WeakVerbs.yml were transcribed from that project's SKILL.md, which
enumerates them as prose. The rules here are a translation of those lists into
Vale's check syntax, and the replacements attached to the swappable half are
this project's own. The judgment the skill also carries -- what to preserve,
when a hedge is honest, how much to change -- is not reproducible as a rule and
stays with the original.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
awesome-claude-output-styles
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes voice definitions shaped after the output styles
catalogued in awesome-claude-output-styles
(https://github.com/smixs/awesome-claude-output-styles), Copyright (c) 2026
Serge Shima, licensed under the MIT License.

Direct, Plain, Unslop, Brevity, Simple and GenZ each take the constraint its
entry describes -- a word budget, a density budget, a required section, a
reading grade -- and state it as a Vale rule. Where a voice enumerates
vocabulary, the terms are in general use and were listed independently.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Basic English
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Simple/Vocabulary.yml checks against the 850-word vocabulary of Basic English,
devised by C. K. Ogden and published in 1930. The dictionary in
Voices/styles/config/dictionaries/ is that list expanded to the regular
inflections the system allows, plus the closed class of pronouns and
determiners Ogden treats as grammar rather than vocabulary. A word list is not
a copyrightable work; it is reproduced here as the specification of a
constraint.
